**19.8. Expansions for \(x\) Large and \(a\) Moderate**

When \(x>>|a|\)

**19.8.1**: \(U(a,\,x)\sim e^{-{\frac{1}{2}}x^{-a-1}}\left\{1\frac{(a+{\frac{1}{2}})(a+{ \frac{3}{2}})}{2x^{2}}\right.\)

\[\left.+\frac{(a+{\frac{1}{2}})(a+{\frac{3}{2}})(a+{\frac{3}{2}})(a+{ \frac{3}{2}})}{2\cdot 4x^{4}}\right.\;\ldots\;\Big{\}}\]
**19.8.2**: \(V(a,\,x)\sim\sqrt{2}\varepsilon^{{\frac{3}{2}}\varepsilon^{{\frac{3}{2}} \varepsilon^{{\frac{3}{2}}}}}\left\{1+\frac{(a-{\frac{1}{2}})(a-{\frac{3}{2}})}{2x^{2}}\right.\]

These expansions form the basis for the choice of standard solutions in **19.3**. The former is valid for complex \(x\), with \(|{\rm arg}\;x|<{\frac{1}{2\pi}}\), in the complete sense of Watson [19.6], although valid for a wider range of \(|{\rm arg}\;x|\) in Poincare's sense; the second series is completely valid _only for x real and positive._

